  <section xml:id="reference-deployment-manual-registration-extensions">
    <title>Extensions</title>
    <para>
      After successful registration of the base system, you can register additional extensions.
    </para>
    <variablelist>
      <title>Extensions for the &productname; &productnumber; family</title>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>&sleha; Extension &productnumber;</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            The &sleha; extension provides mature, industry-leading open-source high-availability
            clustering technologies that are easy to set up and use. It can be deployed in physical
            and/or virtual environments, and can cluster physical servers, virtual servers, or any
            combination of the two to suit the needs of your business.
          </para>
          <para>
            To register your &sleha; extension, enter its registration code and click
            <guilabel>Register</guilabel>.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>&ph; &productnumber;</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            &ph; is a free-of-charge module providing access to community-maintained packages built
            to run on &productname;. Built from the same sources used in &osuse; distributions,
            these quality packages provide additional software to what is found in the &productname;
            product. The packages in this module are delivered without L3 support but do not
            interfere with the supportability of &productname;.
          </para>
          <para>
            To register with the &ph;, click <guilabel>Register</guilabel>.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
    <note>
      <title>Trusting the &ph; signing key</title>
      <para>
        If you enable the &ph;, you will be asked to trust the signing key of that repository.
      </para>
    </note>
  </section>
</topic>
